# mod-custom-spells: the Hunter lines of the third concept list
# (operator 2026-10-31; share-public
# custom-spells/records/2026-10-31-third-concept-list.md), wave 1 = the
# spell modifiers, wave 2 = procs and stacking buffs (900574 Random Traps,
# 900575 Trap Echo). Every check states the list's line, so a FAIL marks a
# defect.
# Test ground: map 13, the FL dummy arena - eight AoE Training Dummies
# (920018) on a 4-yd circle around (-270, 150); d1 = the west-most one. The
# bot stands west of the ring facing it.
# Spells: Explosive Trap 49067 (effect 49065: a hit and a burn), Immolation
# Trap 49056 (effect 51740: a burn). Wave 2: Frost Trap 13809 (its effect, the
# ground aura, is 13810), Serpent Sting 49001 (a DoT keeps the hunter in
# combat while it ticks; Serpent Sting needs the target in front, so the hunter
# `approach`es d1 first - standing 3 yd west of d1 an Explosive Trap still
# reaches the ring's dummies, at least 5 of the 8 per cast).
name    Custom spells - Hunter third list
timeout 300s

bot hu hunter slot=4

place 13 -279 150 -423.2 0
require hu alive
pick d1 creature:920018 near hu
require d1 exists
do gm target hu
as gm .unlearn 900573
do hu learn 49067
do hu learn 49056

log Control - without the passive the traps are unmodified
expect hu spellmod 49065 damage 100 == 100
expect hu spellmod 51740 dot 100 == 100

log Survival - 900573 "traps +50% damage": Explosive Trap's hit and burn, Immolation Trap's burn
do hu learn 900573
expect hu spellmod 49065 damage 100 == 150
expect hu spellmod 49065 dot 100 == 150
expect hu spellmod 51740 dot 100 == 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wave 2
log Survival - 900574 "auto cast a random trap every 5 seconds while in combat": Explosive Trap is the only trap the hunter knows (Immolation unlearned), so the trap that goes off is the Explosive Trap Effect 49065 - out of combat nothing goes off in 6 s (the first tick is 5 s after the passive is learned)
as gm .unlearn 900574
as gm .unlearn 900575
as gm .unlearn 49056
do hu learn 49001
do hu goto -270 150 -423.2
wait 500ms
do hu learn 900574
spelllog start
wait 6s
spelllog stop
expect hu outofcombat
expect hu spell 49065 casts == 0

log Survival - 900574 in combat (a Serpent Sting ticking on d1) two ticks, 5 s and 10 s after the passive, each throw the Explosive Trap Effect (3 ticks at most in the window)
as gm .unlearn 900574
do hu approach d1 3
wait 300ms
do hu learn 900574
do hu cast 49001 on d1 triggered
waitfor hu incombat timeout 3s
spelllog start
wait 4s
do hu cast 49001 on d1 triggered
wait 4s
do hu cast 49001 on d1 triggered
wait 3s
spelllog stop
expect hu incombat
expect hu spell 49065 casts >= 2
expect hu spell 49065 casts <= 3
expect hu spell 49065 targets >= 10

log Survival - 900574 every trap kind goes off the same way: with Frost Trap the only trap known (Explosive unlearned) the Frost Trap Effect (13810, the slowing ground aura) is cast
as gm .unlearn 900574
as gm .unlearn 49067
do hu learn 13809
do hu approach d1 3
wait 300ms
do hu learn 900574
do hu cast 49001 on d1 triggered
waitfor hu incombat timeout 3s
spelllog start
wait 3s
do hu cast 49001 on d1 triggered
wait 3s
spelllog stop
expect hu spell 13810 casts >= 1
as gm .unlearn 900574
as gm .unlearn 13809
do hu learn 49067

log Survival - 900575 "when a trap triggers, it has a 25% chance to spawn another trap": 40 Explosive Trap Effects (49065, cast by the hunter itself in the ring's middle - a trap's effect is a triggered cast that raises the trap activation event) - each has a 25 % chance for a second one at the same spot, but a second one never spawns a third: 42 to 80 casts (P(fewer than 2 echoes) below 0.1 %)
do hu learn 900575
do hu goto -270 150 -423.2
wait 500ms
spelllog start
do hu cast 49065 triggered
wait 120ms
do hu cast 49065 triggered
wait 120ms
do hu cast 49065 triggered
wait 120ms
do hu cast 49065 triggered
wait 120ms
do hu cast 49065 triggered
wait 120ms
